  "spoken_content": [
    {
      "start_seconds": 0,
      "end_seconds": 3,
      "text": "Here's everything I eat in a day to feel snatched instead of bloated as a 25 year old.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 3,
      "end_seconds": 9,
      "text": "Boy, um, if that is not a wildly obvious body check, I really do not know what is.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 9,
      "end_seconds": 18,
      "text": "But here's my friendly reminder to all of you folks, that you can do all the same things that she does to look snatched and still not look like her.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 18,
      "end_seconds": 25,
      "text": "But I'm Abbey Sharp, I'm the internet's no BS dietitian. Let's take a look see at some of these hot diet tips to get snatched.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 25,
      "end_seconds": 26,
      "text": "Some eggs and sourdough toast.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 26,
      "end_seconds": 30,
      "text": "Alright, so we got lots of protein from the egg whites and some fibre from the sourdough.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 30,
      "end_seconds": 39,
      "text": "Both eggs and sourdough are very good options if you are feeling bloated or are susceptible to bloating because they are very gentle on the gut.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 39,
      "end_seconds": 52,
      "text": "But I would highly recommend keeping at least one or two yolks in that egg kind of scramble. That's going to add some healthy fats, some choline, antioxidants, and vitamin D, and also not likely to cause bloating.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 52,
      "end_seconds": 54,
      "text": "Cream of rice and mix in some peanut butter.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 54,
      "end_seconds": 105,
      "text": "Okay, so cream of wheat is also a very gentle soothing meal for your gut, but it's gentle because there's not a whole lot going on here. Like there's zero fibre, only two grams of protein, and also is very low calorie.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 105,
      "end_seconds": 115,
      "text": "Yes, bloating can be caused by excess fibre, especially high FODMAP fibre foods, but a lot of the time it's actually from constipation.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 115,
      "end_seconds": 124,
      "text": "So we ideally want to identify the precise FODMAP triggers while still meeting our fibre needs from less triggering sources.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 124,
      "end_seconds": 132,
      "text": "So for example, research has found that kiwi fruit not only can help with constipation but can also help with bloating.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 132,
      "end_seconds": 142,
      "text": "You can also up the protein in this meal by adding a scoop of like a gut-friendly protein powder or making it with a higher protein milk like pea, soy, or a lactose-free cow's milk if that's tolerated.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 142,
      "end_seconds": 148,
      "text": "For lunch I was craving beef and I didn't have any gluten-free buns at home, so lettuce wraps had to do. I added some egg.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 148,
      "end_seconds": 153,
      "text": "Alright, we got lots of protein in the egg and the burger, but again, very little carbs and fibre.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 153,
      "end_seconds": 202,
      "text": "Now if gluten is a concern, pairing the burger with another source of like a low FODMAP fibre like sweet potatoes or quinoa would be a really great option.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 202,
      "end_seconds": 205,
      "text": "Ground beef with veggies, rice and beans.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 205,
      "end_seconds": 217,
      "text": "Uh yum. This looks like an amazing hunger crushing combo here. We got loads of protein in the beef and the beans. We got a little bit of fibre in the beans and the veggies and probably some kind of healthy fats maybe in the cooking oil.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 217,
      "end_seconds": 235,
      "text": "Now beans can be a common bloating trigger because they have these hard to digest fibres. So using like an alpha galactosidase digestive enzyme can potentially help if you are struggling with that. And PS, Neue Theories Digestion Bloat is now 60% off while supplies last. So just a shameless plug because this is your last chance to get it.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 235,
      "end_seconds": 238,
      "text": "Coconut milk mint ice cream before bed.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 238,
      "end_seconds": 249,
      "text": "Okay, I've never heard of this brand, but if you value an ice cream with a very minimal ingredient list, this looks like a really great choice that is sweetened without any kind of sugar alcohols, which can be a major bloating culprit for a lot of folks.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 249,
      "end_seconds": 300,
      "text": "Friends, I have zero issue with any of these meals, like they're protein rich, they're nutrient dense, and for the most part, they're totally valid choices for sensitive tummies.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    },
    {
      "start_seconds": 300,
      "end_seconds": 333,
      "text": "But when gut healing is packaged with a body check and framed around looking snatched, it tends to blur the line between health and aesthetics. And speaking as someone with IBS who has dealt with very painful bloating for years, people with IBS need real solutions that are not sneakily wrapped up in diet culture. So let's not co-opt gut health language to sell what may actually just be another body ideal. Stay fueled, friends. Next.",
      "language": "English",
      "confidence": null
    }
  ],
